{"id":"5-tom","name":"5-TOM","form":"capsule","status":"Reference","source":"Wikidata","wikidata":"Q123582470","aliases":"","category":"Stimulant","chemicalClass":"Substituted phenethylamines","groups":[],"atc":[],"summary":"5-TOM, also known as 2-methoxy-4-methyl-5-methylthioamphetamine or as 5-thio-DOM, is a psychedelic drug of the phenethylamine and amphetamine families related to the DOx psychedelic DOM. It is the analogue of DOM in which the methoxy group at the 5 position has been replaced with a methylthio group. The drug is one of two possible TOM (thio-DOM) positional isomers, the other being 2-TOM.","summarySources":"Wikipedia","doseUnit":"","doseRows":[],"durationRows":[],"subjectiveEffects":[],"combinations":[],"citations":[],"helpfulLinks":[{"title":"Wikipedia","description":"Encyclopedia article","url":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/5-TOM"},{"title":"Wikidata","description":"Structured data on 5-TOM","url":"https://www.wikidata.org/wiki/Q123582470"},{"title":"PubChem","description":"Chemistry, safety and literature","url":"https://pubchem.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/compound/15915349"}],"formula":"C12H19NOS","molarMass":225.35,"pharmacology":{"kind":"Serotonergic psychedelic; Hallucinogen","body":[{"what":"onset","says":"30 minutes; Peak: ~3 hours"},{"what":"lasts","says":"6–10 hours (but up to 12–16 hours)"}],"figures":"5-TOM"},"uses":{"routes":"Oral","figures":"5-TOM"}}